  {
   "t": 30.75,
   "kind": "thought",
   "data": {
    "text": "In `lagos-lekki-v2`, 120mm / 3h over the whole area.\n\nBaseline run `r_a9cb390eab1dd07f` vs tide-lock run `r_532da7dbd6b3a6a5` with `tide boundary_level_m = 1.0`:\n\n> Tide level is an assumed lagoon / sea level, not a forecast.\n\n### Flooded buildings - whole area\n\nBaseline:\n* `buildings_flooded`: 29,137\n* `buildings_flooded_severe`: 8,230\n* `people_exposed`: 88,124\n* `road_km_impassable`: 384.7 km\n* `flooded_area_km2`: 21.86 km2\n* `max_depth_m`: 2.051 m\n\n1 m tide-lock:\n* `buildings_flooded`: 29,567 = +430 / +1.5%\n* `buildings_flooded_severe`: 8,585 = +355 / +4.3%\n* `people_exposed`: 90,212 = +2,088 / +2.4%\n* `road_km_impassable`: 430.07 km = +45.37 km / +11.8%\n* `flooded_area_km2`: 28.51 km2 = +6.65 km2 / +30.4%\n* `max_depth_m`: 2.064 m = +0.013 m\n\nMechanism in the water balance:\n* `stored_volume_end_m3`: 7,335,884 -> 13,827,731\n* `boundary_outflow_m3`: +1,543,335 -> -4,992,828\n\nNegative outflow = net inflow from the boundary. The high lagoon blocks drainage and spreads water over low margins, so flooded area and impassable roads grow much faster than building count.\n\n### Where\n\nOne change at a time, checked by neighbourhood:\n\n* `area:Ikate:buildings_flooded`: 811 -> 842 (+31)\n* `area:Ikate:max_depth_m`: 0.751 -> 1.230 m\n* `area:Ikate:flooded_area_km2`: 0.554 -> 0.767 km2\n\n* `area:Jakande:buildings_flooded`: 1,534 -> 1,536, `area:Jakande:max_depth_m` 1.13 -> 1.158 m - essentially unchanged.\n* `area:Lekki Phase 1:buildings_flooded`: 1,555 -> 1,555 - no change.\n* `area:Chisco:buildings_flooded`: 937 -> 937 - no change.\n\nTide-lock impact is coastal / lagoon-margin, e.g. Ikate, not uniform inland.\n\n### Evacuation route to nearest shelter\n\nTested from Ikate centroid `[3.4874,6.42637]`:\n\nAt peak `t_s=10200s`:\n* baseline `rt_c990b70e23ee`: `reachable: false`, 2,563 edges removed\n* 1m lock `rt_07446ba4af66`: `reachable: false`, 2,886 edges removed\n\nNo through route to nearest shelter at peak in either case; tide-lock removes ~323 more road segments.\n\nAt early `t_s=3600s`:\n* baseline `rt_a062f5de5c10`: reachable to `Unnamed place of worship (candidate shelter (assumed))`, 2.545 km, 38.2 min, 20 edges removed\n* 1m lock `rt_062d957f93b8`: reachable to same shelter, same 2.545 km path, 38.2 min, 344 edges removed\n\nRoute stays open early but with far less redundancy under tide-lock. Plan for earlier departure from coastal pockets like Ikate when the lagoon is held high.\n"
   }
  },
